{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791104780,"nonce":"E2vjyqxG0bAPJRRNg9gedIMBzDI=","title":"Visual debugger for ashui","message":"A debugger that ships with ashui: see what the UI did, frame by frame, and why, for people and for agents reviewing frames. Blinc splits the same idea into blinc_recorder (capture: events, tree snapshots, visual props; sessions; replay; a debug server; headless frame sequences and regression) and blinc_debugger (an app: element tree with diffs, preview with overlay, inspector, event timeline).\n\nFoundation, landed with this issue cited: ashui.debug's motion trace.\n- MotionTrace/MotionTrack: every property tween (CSS and Tw transitions), @keyframes run, FLIP layout animation and spring recorded as declared (property, from, to, delay, duration, curve) and as it ran, a sample per frame on the scheduler's clock, plus the element's drawn rect per frame.\n- MotionCheck: verdicts. Start lag, off-curve distance against the declared curve at the scheduler's clock, actual vs declared duration, jumps, snaps (declared, did not animate), a move repeated after it completed, moves from a value to itself, springs against the damped oscillator's closed form, overshoot.\n- MotionOverlay (an Offscreen FrameOverlay, own tree): outlines, trails a dot a frame, progress bars with the expected tick, labels, a curve panel.\n- MotionRecorder: scripted recordings to .ashui/snapshots/motion/\u003cname\u003e/ (frames, filmstrip, curves, report.txt, trace.json, an events.log line).\n- MotionStream: ASHUI_MOTION=overlay|stream in WindowedApp; stream writes each burst of motion as a recording, stepping animation time a fixed 1/60 per captured frame.\n\nNext, roughly in order:\n- Snaps the trace cannot see: a property a CSS transition covers that changes with no tween at all (the switch thumb and accordion chevron do this today). Needs a hook where Css applies a transitioned property.\n- Keyframes: judge each segment's easing, not only the timeline.\n- Input event capture and replay (pointer, keys, focus) into the same session, so a recording can be replayed deterministically and diffed.\n- Tree snapshots per frame and diffs (what was added, removed, restyled), with CSS provenance (which rule set a value).\n- An inspector overlay: hover an element, see its box model, computed CSS, interaction state.\n- A timeline UI built in ashui: tracks, events, frames scrubbable.\n- A debug server so a running app can be attached to from another process (the debugger app, or an agent).\n- Frame regression: compare a recording against a stored one.","files":null}]}